 "turns": [
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Hello there! How's your day treating you?",
   "est_sec": 2.27,
   "gap_before": 0.48,
   "role": "greeting",
   "phrasing": "greet_25"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "I'm well, thanks.",
   "est_sec": 1.03,
   "gap_before": 0.81,
   "event": "greeting_answer",
   "phrasing": "greet_ans_25"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Every Swiss roll I make cracks when I roll it up.",
   "est_sec": 3.51,
   "gap_before": 0.57,
   "event": "ordinary_request",
   "block": "baking.dlg26"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Are you rolling it while it's still warm?",
   "est_sec": 2.58,
   "gap_before": 0.73,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "baking.dlg26"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "No, I let it cool first so the cream doesn't melt.",
   "est_sec": 3.51,
   "gap_before": 1.42,
   "event": "ordinary_request",
   "block": "baking.dlg26"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "That's the trick most people miss. Roll the sponge up warm in a clean tea towel without any filling, let it cool in that shape, then unroll and fill.",
   "est_sec": 9.09,
   "gap_before": 0.64,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "baking.dlg26"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "So it sort of",
   "est_sec": 1.34,
   "gap_before": 0.47,
   "event": "distractor",
   "kind": "pause",
   "block": "baking.dlg26"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "remembers the shape?",
   "est_sec": 1.03,
   "gap_before": 2.4,
   "event": "ordinary_request",
   "block": "baking.dlg26"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Exactly. The sponge sets in the curl, so it won't fight you later. Also bake it just until it springs back, an overbaked sponge cracks easily.",
   "est_sec": 8.16,
   "gap_before": 0.81,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "baking.dlg26"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "My mum is going to be so impressed.",
   "est_sec": 2.58,
   "gap_before": 2.67,
   "block": "baking.dlg26"
  }
 ]
}
